{
 "name": "winged biped (Tidewrack wyvern), with Tidewrack's own jaw mask",
 "comment": "Identical to winged-biped.json except jaw_mask (that file's null mask kept heat weights, which on Tidewrack gave the jaw bone the tip of the snout and a share of the skull top behind the hinge: a jaw rotation flipped the nose up and left the mandible). The plane below was measured on Tidewrack's own mouth cavity in canonical space (vertical ray crossings at |x|<=0.03, y 0.28-0.42; canonical(co) = (co - bone_fit_bias) / bone_fit_scale from artifacts/tidewrack/build_stats.json); see artifacts/tidewrack/jaw-mask/README.md. Bone head/tail in the rigger frame: Blender Z-up after its 180-degree Z turn, +Y forward (snout), left = -X. reference_bounds is the Stormsail mesh bbox measured in that frame (the rigger remaps onto the Tidewrack bbox). Two hind legs plus wing forelimbs; no upper_arm/forearm/wrist/hand/toe_fore bones. Four finger ribs per wing, the tail ends in a rudder fin (tail_10, tail_11).",
