  "type": "plane",
  "comment": "Canonical (y,z); the hinge (jaw bone head) is at y .30, z .583 and the head is carried high over the chest (head z .52-.68, chest/neck top below .50 ahead of y .31). Cheek solid to y .315, then cavity windows [mandible top, palate] over |x|<=.02: y .32 [.5919,.5948], .33 [.5891,.5978], .34 [.5828,.5892], .35 [.5747,.5853], .36 [.5681,.5802], .37 [.5618,.5795], .38 [.5522,.5752]; the mandible ends at y .385 and the snout underside is .573 at .39, .570 at .40, .568 at .41. The mandible hangs steeper (-0.66) than the palate (-0.30), so the line is shallow behind the teeth and steep along the gape: 3 points, -0.27 then -0.56, extrapolated at both ends. Behind the hinge the first segment runs at z .60-.61, where heat's jaw weight on the skull is already below 0.2, so the box starts at the head bone (y .26) and reclaim_above takes the skull top and the snout back from the jaw bone; the jowl under the hinge (jaw 0.3-0.66) is left to heat because any boundary through it would be a larger step. z_min .51 sits between the neck top at y .31 (.5004) and the chin tip (.5261). x_max .12 clears the head frills (|x| .101) and nothing else lives in the box.",
